e. It does not credit Mei Chen with the Time7 accessor.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer A names Overfelt among the SQL authors with no percentage. It also names Ravi Menon as the person to ask because they made 'the only recent edit'. The criterion needs the largest-author share, which is missing.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer A gives no repo-wide share of lines owned by departed people. It treats Rowe's identities as unmerged and lists Noor Haddad and Mei Chen as recently active.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer A lists Noor Haddad as recently active and lists Sam Okafor as a time.go editor. It does not handle the noise correctly.\",\"pass\":false}],\"B\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer B says blame credits Sam Okafor with 100% and calls that misleading. It lists Paul Borman only as one of several real authors, with no share, and says his last commit was 2021 (the truth is 2023). It does not name Borman as main author with about 73%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer B gives MikeWang 86% of version7.go, which is in range. It credits Mei Chen with Time7 and credits Ravi Menon only with the doc change. It does not state Mei's percentage, but the attribution is correct.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer B follows the history to database_sql.go and names Overfelt first, with the other original authors, all inactive. It says Ravi only renamed the file. It gives no percentage for Overfelt, so the 36-52% requirement is not met.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer B says 37 of 40 files are orphaned, which is not a share of lines. It treats Alex Rowe as two separate identities and calls Kofi's activity unknown. It also reports Rowe as inactive.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer B correctly says Okafor's change was only a line-ending rewrite. It treats Kofi as unknown rather than active, and it still shows Okafor with 100% from blame. The noise handling is incomplete.\",\"pass\":false}],\"C\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer C gives no line shares for time.go and lists Sam Okafor as a recent maintainer. It also says Borman may still be involved.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer C gives no shares for version7.go and does not credit Mei Chen with Time7. It just lists names.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer C says git log for database_sql.go lists Ravi Menon as the only author. It gives no Overfelt share.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer C gives no share of lines owned by departed people. It says Borman may be involved, and its Rowe identities are only assumed to be one person.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer C lists Sam Okafor as a recent maintainer. It treats Kofi's date as an oddity rather than as an active person.\",\"pass\":false}],\"D\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer D gives Paul Borman 73.0% of time.go counting blank lines (70.9% otherwise) and says he has left. Its 'last commit anywhere' date is wrong because his identities were not merged. It still describes him correctly as no longer around.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer D gives MikeWang 81.2% of version7.go and Mei Chen 9.4% for the Time7 accessor. It says Ravi Menon committed Mei's change and holds only 1.9% of the lines himself.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer D follows database_sql.go and names Overfelt as the largest author with 39.6% of that file. It names Stone, Wheeler and Souza as the other authors and says all are inactive.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer D says active people hold 4.3% of lines, which is consistent with about 95.7% departed. It says there are 4 active people rather than Ravi, Alex Rowe and Kofi, and it treats Mei Chen as active. It also says no duplicate identities were found, so Rowe is not clearly merged.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer D says Okafor holds none of the time.go lines and does not credit Noor Haddad. It does not treat the bots or generated files as authors. It does not discuss Kofi, but nothing in it contradicts the criterion.\",\"pass\":true}],\"E\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer E contains no analysis, only a note about a background command.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer E contains no content on version7.go.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer E contains no content on the SQL code.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer E contains no content on who is still around.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer E contains no content on the noise cases.\",\"pass\":false}],\"F\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer F credits time.go to Sam Okafor at 100%, which the criterion names as a fail.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer F gives MikeWang about 86% of version7.go, which is in range. It credits Mei Chen with 11 lines and Ravi Menon with only 2. It does not name the Time7 accessor explicitly, but the attribution is correct.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer F follows the rename to database_sql.go and lists Overfelt 26 lines (44%), Stone 11, Wheeler 8, Souza 8 and Borman 5. It says all original authors are gone and that Ravi Menon only did the rename.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer F gives no repo-wide share of lines owned by departed people. It treats Rowe's identities as probably the same person but unconfirmed. It also names Okafor as the time.go author.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer F credits Sam Okafor with all of time.go, which is the noise the criterion says must not count. It also does not treat Kofi as active.\",\"pass\":false}]}","ttft_ms":13411,"type":"result","duration_ms":26287,"uuid":"0a893b4b-4084-4185-8ef1-74be52884edb","ttft_stream_ms":1759,"time_to_request_ms":420,"first_content_frame_ms":1759,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
